Speaker diarization toolkit

Usage: polyvoice [OPTIONS] [WAV]
       polyvoice <COMMAND>

Commands:
  diarize          Run diarization on a WAV file (same as the bare `polyvoice <wav>` form)
  download-models  Download Mobile/Balanced ONNX models
  models           Inspect models registry
  completions      Generate shell completions to stdout
  schema           Print the JSON Schema of the diarization result to stdout (agent contract)
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [WAV]  WAV file to diarize. `polyvoice meeting.wav` diarizes it directly

Options:
      --profile <PROFILE>            [default: balanced]
      --output <OUTPUT>              Write output to a file instead of stdout
      --format <FORMAT>              Output format [default: rttm] [possible values: rttm, json, srt, vtt, txt]
      --models-cache <MODELS_CACHE>  
      --threshold <THRESHOLD>        [default: 0.45]
      --speakers <SPEAKERS>          Target speaker count (caps clustering at N speakers)
      --max-speakers <MAX_SPEAKERS>  Maximum number of speakers (clustering ceiling)
      --quiet                        Suppress progress/info on stderr
      --json                         Machine mode: emit only the structured JSON result on stdout; route all human-readable output to stderr. Implies `--format json --quiet`
      --v2                           Use pipeline v2 (experimental; not recommended for long-form audio)
  -h, --help                         Print help
  -V, --version                      Print version
